    "body": "Adds onchain (Bitcoin) mint and melt support per [NUT-30](https://github.com/cashubtc/nuts/pull/365).\r\n\r\n## What's new\r\n\r\n### Onchain minting\r\n- `Wallet.createMintQuoteOnchain(pubkey)` / `Mint.createMintQuoteOnchain(...)`, request a pubkey-locked onchain mint quote\r\n- `Wallet.checkMintQuoteOnchain(quote)` / `Mint.checkMintQuoteOnchain(...)`\r\n- `Wallet.mintProofsOnchain(amount, quote, privkey, ...)` / `Mint.mintOnchain(...)`\r\n- `WalletOps.mintOnchain(amount, quote)` builder\r\n\r\nOnchain mint quotes are **locked to a public key**. The quote response carries `amount_paid` and `amount_issued` so callers can mint incrementally as on-chain funds confirm; a guard prevents over-minting a partially-paid quote.\r\n\r\n### Onchain melting\r\n- `Wallet.createMeltQuoteOnchain(address, amount)` / `Mint.createMeltQuoteOnchain(...)`\r\n- `Wallet.checkMeltQuoteOnchain(quote)` / `Mint.checkMeltQuoteOnchain(...)`\r\n- `Wallet.meltProofsOnchain(quote, proofs, estimatedBlocks, ...)` / `Mint.meltOnchain(...)`\r\n- `WalletOps.meltOnchain(quote, proofs)` -> `MeltOnchainBuilder` (`.estimatedBlocks()`, `.keyset()`, `.privkey()`, `.run()`)\r\n\r\nA melt quote returns a **single quote with multiple `fee_options`** (each pairing a `fee_reserve` with `estimated_blocks`); the fee tier is selected at execution time. The response exposes `selected_estimated_blocks` and `outpoint` once broadcast. NUT-08 change is supported on onchain melt.\r\n\r\n### Supporting changes\r\n- `MintMethod` extended with `'onchain'`; `MintBuilder`/`MintQuoteFor` updated accordingly\r\n- New types: `MintQuoteOnchain{Request,Response}`, `MeltQuoteOnchain{Request,Response}`, `MeltQuoteOnchainFeeOption` (`src/model/types/NUT30.ts`)\r\n- `completeMelt` now takes a `CompleteMeltOptions` object (`preferAsync`, `extraPayload`); the positional `preferAsync` overload is kept and `@deprecated`\r\n- `MeltProofsResponse` now exposes `outputData`, so deferred NUT-08 change can be recovered\r\n- `prepareMelt` config widened to `PrepareMeltConfig` (adds `nut08Change`)\r\n- `SwapMethod.options` gains `confirmations`\r\n- Onchain methods carry an `@experimental` tag pending NUT-30 finalization\r\n\r\n### Examples & docs\r\n- New interactive `examples/onchain_example.ts` (listed in `examples/README.md`)\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\nUnit and node integration coverage for onchain mint/melt across `Mint`, `Wallet`, and `WalletOps`.\r\n",
